# One record per line: path version mode canonical provenance
#
# version     the file's (version ...) stamp, or - when it has none
# mode        normal | compact | library-table | json | oracle
# canonical   yes when the file is a fixed point of its prettifier mode, and -
#             when the question does not apply
# provenance  kicad-cli when KiCad wrote the bytes, hand when we did
#
# An oracle is KiCad's own answer about a fixture beside it, or our prediction
# that KiCad confirmed. It is data, not a schematic, so it has no stamp and no
# prettifier mode. Regenerate an oracle from inside its own directory: the ERC
# JSON records the source file name, and a run from elsewhere writes a path.
#
# sch/nets/nets_channel.kicad_sch is deliberately NOT canonicalised. It is a
# child sheet placed twice, and `kicad-cli sch upgrade` run on a child on its
# own prunes the instance paths of every placement but one, which is exactly
# the data the fixture exists to carry.
#
# Files named MANIFEST or *.manifest are records, not fixtures, and are skipped.
#
# Identifiers were rewritten once, by the fixture-handle chore (D1, 2026-08-21).
# Every fixture had put its per-object variation in the LAST field of its uuid,
# so every object of every fixture answered to the same eight-character handle
# `00000000` and no committed fixture could exercise a command addressed by one.
# Each identifier keeps its old body and gains a leading `{series:02x}{n:06x}`
# — the format the probe crate uses (kicli-probe/src/drawing.rs) — with the
# series raised above 0x0f so a committed fixture cannot collide with a probe
# drawing, which numbers its series from 1. Nothing else about any file moved.
#
# The `kicad-cli` provenance below still holds, and was re-verified rather than
# assumed: under KICLI_TEST_KICAD_CLI the geometry ERC oracles, both netlists
# and the routing calibration fixture are regenerated by KiCad itself and match
# the committed bytes. `sch/routing/calibration.kicad_sch` is the one file whose
# identifiers were NOT touched: it is byte-compared against what the probe
# recipe builds, and its root sheet uuid is the probe crate's `ROOT` constant.
